WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.660
It's May 13th, 2026.

00:00:03.500 --> 00:00:09.060
Today's AI news is pretty exciting, and I promise, no jargon, let's go.

00:00:09.960 --> 00:00:15.360
So imagine your favorite video game suddenly switches from giving you cheat codes to actually

00:00:15.360 --> 00:00:18.120
teaching you the rules so you can win on your own.

00:00:18.820 --> 00:00:24.980
That is basically what OpenAI just made easier with a hidden feature called Study Mode inside

00:00:24.980 --> 00:00:26.080
chat GPT.

00:00:26.940 --> 00:00:34.120
You reach it by typing a simple slash command like slash study or slash learn at the start

00:00:34.120 --> 00:00:34.880
of any chat.

00:00:35.640 --> 00:00:40.720
Think of it like flipping a switch that changes the AI from a quick answer machine into

00:00:40.720 --> 00:00:45.840
a patient tutor who asks you questions and checks what you actually understand.

00:00:46.680 --> 00:00:51.860
Instead of handing over a full solution to your homework, it breaks the problem into small

00:00:51.860 --> 00:00:53.920
pieces and waits for your responses.

00:00:54.920 --> 00:01:00.980
This matters for school because most students use AI to finish assignments fast, yet

00:01:00.980 --> 00:01:04.460
this version pushes you to learn the material step by step.

00:01:05.100 --> 00:01:10.900
It can help with anything from algebra proves to writing essays by giving hints instead

00:01:10.900 --> 00:01:11.920
of complete answers.

00:01:12.680 --> 00:01:18.520
For you personally, it means free tutoring help at 10 at night the day before a test,

00:01:18.980 --> 00:01:20.760
without waiting for a human tutor.

00:01:20.760 --> 00:01:26.460
The shortcuts work on both the web version and the mobile app so you can try them during

00:01:26.460 --> 00:01:28.700
study hall or on the bus ride home.

00:01:29.340 --> 00:01:37.580
To test it yourself, open chat GPT, start a new chat and type slash study followed by your

00:01:37.580 --> 00:01:41.960
topic like quadratic equations or how photosynthesis works.

00:01:42.760 --> 00:01:47.240
Then answer the questions it asks instead of asking it to do the work for you.

00:01:49.100 --> 00:01:54.120
Okay, now for my favorite part of the show, the deep dive where we look under the hood.

00:01:55.040 --> 00:02:01.080
Today's topic is AI Agents, which sounds fancy but works a lot like a video game character

00:02:01.080 --> 00:02:01.780
you control.

00:02:02.760 --> 00:02:08.460
You know how in a game your character can open doors, fight enemies and collect items even

00:02:08.460 --> 00:02:10.940
though it has no idea it is inside a game.

00:02:10.940 --> 00:02:16.820
It simply follows the rules the programmers gave it and reacts to whatever button you press.

00:02:17.540 --> 00:02:23.860
An AI agent on your phone does something similar except it learned every possible button sequence

00:02:23.860 --> 00:02:25.940
by watching millions of examples.

00:02:26.920 --> 00:02:33.160
First it reads the screen the way you would, then it picks the next tiny action like tapping

00:02:33.160 --> 00:02:35.080
a date picker or typing an address.

00:02:36.040 --> 00:02:42.480
Each small step happens so fast it feels like one smooth task whether that is booking a ride

00:02:42.480 --> 00:02:49.320
or filling out a form the agent is not thinking or planning like a person it is extremely good at

00:02:49.320 --> 00:02:56.520
copying successful sequences it has seen before. So next time someone says AI agent you can picture

00:02:56.520 --> 00:03:02.780
it as a super fast video game character that learned every level by watching millions of players and

00:03:02.780 --> 00:03:07.440
that is basically how these agents work. Not so scary once you see the pattern right.

00:03:10.080 --> 00:03:12.960
Now let's look at some cool stuff you can actually try.

00:03:13.860 --> 00:03:20.940
Google added new features called Gemini Intelligence to recent Android phones that let the AI handle

00:03:20.940 --> 00:03:27.220
real multi-step jobs. Think of it like having a helpful assistant sitting next to you who can see

00:03:27.220 --> 00:03:34.940
your screen and offer to finish the boring parts. It can summarize long web pages rewrite rough voice

00:03:34.940 --> 00:03:41.540
notes into clean text messages or even help book travel by filling forms step by step.

00:03:42.560 --> 00:03:47.400
Anyone with a recent Android phone can start right away without extra apps.

00:03:48.160 --> 00:03:54.360
Open Chrome on your phone, visit a long article and ask Gemini to summarize it in three bullet

00:03:54.360 --> 00:04:00.560
points or start typing a text message and tap the Gemini button to let it polish your rough thoughts

00:04:00.560 --> 00:04:06.660
while you watch. You stay in control the whole time which makes it feel more like a partner than a

00:04:06.660 --> 00:04:13.640
replacement. Next up is something that feels straight out of a movie. China's unitary company known

00:04:13.640 --> 00:04:21.960
for affordable dancing robots now sells a full-size walking robot called the GD01. It can smash

00:04:21.960 --> 00:04:28.860
through walls and move like a sci-fi character and the fact that regular people can buy one shows how fast

00:04:28.860 --> 00:04:34.640
robot hardware is getting cheaper. If you are into building things or robotics clubs at school

00:04:35.240 --> 00:04:41.820
this is the kind of machine that used to exist only in research labs. You cannot try the real one for

00:04:41.820 --> 00:04:48.580
free but you can watch the official videos on YouTube to see it in action. Imagine what smaller

00:04:48.580 --> 00:04:54.940
versions might do in games or future jobs and you start to see how quickly this technology is moving

00:04:54.940 --> 00:05:02.440
from labs into everyday hands. Time for some quick bits that caught my eye this week.

